    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly. High-density racking systems increase the risk of fire spread when storing flammable solvents due to the greater surface area exposed to potential ignition sources for combustion. The proximity of adjacent containers can lead to intense, rapid combustion if a fire ignites one container; flammable vapors from adjacent tanks can also contribute to the fire's spread, as well as if the fire breaks through container seals or primary containment structures, such as the tank ends or pressure relief devices. Heat conduction between packed tanks can cause premature ignition of unignited containers, further accelerating the fire within the storage area.",
